<title>BAHRAIN: UAE extends $27 million to Bahrain to build houses.</title>
<headline>UAE extends $27 million to Bahrain to build houses.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bahrain on Wednesday signed a memorandum of understanding with the Abu Dhabi Development Fund to finance the building of houses for Bahraini citizens on the island.</p>
<p>The official Gulf News Agency said under the memorandum the United Arab Emirates extended 100 million dirhams ($27 million) to Bahrain to build a residential town named after UAE President Sheikh Zaid bin Sultan al-Nahayan.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
<p>($1=3.67 UAE dirhams)</p>
</text>
